# GitHub Pages reads this file to serve the site on a custom domain.
# The file must contain ONLY the bare hostname, as a single line, with no protocol
# (never https://) and no trailing slash and no path. Anything else in an active
# line breaks the Pages deployment, which is why every line in this file is
# currently commented out.
#
# Uncommenting it and pushing will CHANGE THE SITE URL and will break any
# hardcoded absolute URL. Canonical link tags, og:url meta tags and the sitemap
# all embed the deployment URL, so after you change this file you must re-run
#
#     python scripts/generate_pages.py
#
# so that canonical URLs and the sitemap are regenerated against the new hostname.
# You may also need to update repoUrl in assets/js/config.js, since the
# "Report an issue" and footer GitHub links are built from it.
#
# To activate a custom domain, uncomment exactly one hostname line below, replace
# it with your own domain, and configure the same domain in the repository's
# Settings, Pages, Custom domain field. Remember that the DNS records for the
# domain must point at GitHub Pages before this will resolve.
#
# --- Commented example hostname, on its own line, and nothing else after it: ---
# cybermastery.example.com
